Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.14,0:00:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On that day during summer vacation,\Nyou knew that the school would go adrift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.01,0:00:10.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So why did you still go?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.44,0:00:13.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right, I knew everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.41,0:00:17.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that's why I did—\NI couldn't just leave everyone to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.52,0:00:19.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what was the point?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.22,0:00:21.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.88,0:00:25.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did they ask for your salvation?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.08,0:00:27.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this world a movie theater?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.21,0:00:30.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, this is no ordinary movie theater.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.92,0:00:33.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.83,0:00:36.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's your point of view.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.73,0:00:48.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Skimming through this, it looks like\Nthe whole film was shot from your perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.41,0:00:49.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.69,0:00:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,d-don't have a hidden camera or anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.80,0:00:55.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.35,0:00:59.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then who on earth did this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.35,0:01:01.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't say I know for sure yet,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.12,0:01:06.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but this might be the first world that shows us other worlds.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.41,0:01:09.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This may be some sort of special place.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.06,0:01:11.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you not found Nagara yet?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.49,0:01:16.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been two months!\NWhat the hell have you been doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.35,0:01:18.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sir, yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.14,0:01:20.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He appears to be constantly moving from world to world,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.63,0:01:23.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we can't seem to locate him using the power relics, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.83,0:01:27.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's not capable of coming up with\Nanything that intelligent on his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.41,0:01:29.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must have collaborators working with him!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.98,0:01:33.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are just as guilty!\NFind them, no matter the cost!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.92,0:01:34.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sir, yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.08,0:01:48.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mizuho sure is taking her time. I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.15,0:01:51.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She should be here any moment now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.72,0:01:54.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have some chocolate if you want some.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.53,0:01:55.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.05,0:02:01.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A-A stray dog?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.42,0:02:08.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mmm, you smell good.\NThe sweet smell of chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.88,0:02:11.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It talked!\NThe dog talked!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.42,0:02:14.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shake!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.13,0:02:15.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.07,0:02:16.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sit up!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.66,0:02:20.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Allow me to introduce you. This is Yamabiko.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.73,0:02:26.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds like he drifted into this world, just like us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.99,0:02:34.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said he used to be human,\Nbut suddenly transformed at some point.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.42,0:02:37.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, there, there...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.47,0:02:41.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pleasure to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.75,0:02:45.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A veteran castaway... dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.82,0:02:48.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ugh, that stinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.52,0:02:54.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're a castaway like us,\Ndoes that mean you're also in stasis?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.61,0:02:55.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.71,0:02:58.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why are you a dog?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.39,0:02:59.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it some sort of power?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.01,0:03:04.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dog or not, I'm still myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.07,0:03:05.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see? I haven't—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.93,0:03:10.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So where have you been all this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.72,0:03:14.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was living in the forest, but the storm\Nthat came through drove me out of there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.81,0:03:16.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does he mean Asakaze?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.37,0:03:18.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Most likely.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.34,0:03:20.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.51,0:03:22.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what's causing this drifting?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.39,0:03:25.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That{\i0} I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.71,0:03:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are we ever going to get home?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.45,0:03:36.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Many who came before me attempted to get back to their own world,\Nbut none have been successful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.92,0:03:40.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Though that doesn't mean there's no hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.37,0:03:42.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? So we {\i1}can{\i0} go home?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.37,0:03:43.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.62,0:03:46.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's still time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.43,0:03:52.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It hasn't been a year since you got here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.61,0:03:56.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whew, we're so close to being finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.54,0:03:57.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.77,0:04:00.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just have to collect the material for its core.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.88,0:04:06.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do we really not have to go looking for it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.12,0:04:08.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently it's going to come to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.60,0:04:11.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.80,0:04:13.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How's things?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.93,0:04:17.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure has been a while, hasn't it?\NWhat have you been up to all this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.36,0:04:23.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been hopping between different worlds with Nagara,\Nlooking for the piece we need to get us back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.73,0:04:25.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, why don't we all go home together?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.86,0:04:30.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think we've already given you our answer to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.20,0:04:33.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The outcome is already decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.97,0:04:38.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't go home.\NOur only choice is to live here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.99,0:04:43.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't give me that nonsense about the outcome already being decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.48,0:04:47.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't it up to youngsters like us to keep trying anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.89,0:04:51.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're inside the light right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.01,0:04:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just one step away.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.93,0:04:56.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never imagined there was someone adrift longer than us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.13,0:04:59.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said there was still time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.80,0:05:01.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That we're still connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.33,0:05:02.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.94,0:05:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could he mean that whatever is holding that connection in place\Nmight be somewhere in this world?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.12,0:05:10.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, could be.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.43,0:05:14.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Provided that your power is what created these worlds,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.41,0:05:17.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and that you held this power even in {\i1}our{\i0} world,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.07,0:05:22.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the school might have been\Nsomething akin to another world.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.53,0:05:28.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if that's true, then maybe there's a film of our world in here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.84,0:05:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fact that we weren't the first ones to go adrift,\N and that it happened to others from our school,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.84,0:05:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,might support that theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.60,0:05:39.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys seem to have gotten the wrong impression.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.40,0:05:46.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was also a 3rd-year student at Shiraito Middle School No. 2,{(QC) perhaps join this, but tell me which you chose either way, since the end of this line probs needs some retiming}\Nthe same as all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.01,0:05:48.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? From the same school?\NThen we're classmates?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.83,0:05:50.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you? What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.38,0:05:51.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yamada Kunihiko.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.94,0:05:54.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was there anyone there with that name?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.95,0:05:58.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no surprise that you wouldn't know me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.95,0:06:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See, I enrolled the year that you graduated.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.48,0:06:03.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, then that means...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.03,0:06:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that strange?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.62,0:06:07.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That would mean that you're here from the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.58,0:06:09.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Space-time is flexible.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.60,0:06:13.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long have you been here, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.84,0:06:15.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,5,000 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.67,0:06:22.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But when he says 5,000 years,\Nit just doesn't seem real, does it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.61,0:06:24.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Plus, he turned into a dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.20,0:06:27.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whoa! What just happened?!{Wow, PTSD from when I had glasses. My vision was roughly this bad. - Lann}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.55,0:06:28.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.55,0:06:30.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,S-Sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.56,0:06:32.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.03,0:06:35.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you just do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.93,0:06:41.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is footage of us since we moved to the island.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.47,0:06:43.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fetch.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.52,0:06:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.38,0:06:47.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's try a little experiment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.91,0:06:48.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.41,0:06:53.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is an app I made for video editing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.43,0:07:01.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.34,0:07:03.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure does.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.32,0:07:06.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Any changes to the film also have an effect on the real world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.93,0:07:09.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's experiment a little more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.60,0:07:13.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are the images from that film.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.04,0:07:18.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now we add something else—\Nlike the great Monkey Mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.32,0:07:26.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fascinating, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.88,0:07:30.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By editing two worlds together,\Nwe can create a composite.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.87,0:07:33.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Amazing. You could do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.52,0:07:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Actually, I already tried this once...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.75,0:07:41.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But nothing happened.{QC}{(Timing) I split different, but dunno what to do with this.}{(QC) Let's get Hourglass into the thread for this too, maybe joining the lines is preferable, maybe adding a fade is preferable, idk}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.76,0:07:45.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The only difference now is that you're here taking part in the preview.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.60,0:07:50.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means that simply editing the film doesn't alter the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.61,0:07:54.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The crucial element is whether or not you're here watching it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.41,0:08:00.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, then what would happen if we played it backwards?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.01,0:08:05.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's trouble on the horizon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.63,0:08:07.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure we should be leaving this up to them?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.87,0:08:10.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean those delicate little mice?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.55,0:08:14.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're as pure as can be,\Nand haven't gotten any preferential treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.91,0:08:17.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They need me to watch over them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.45,0:08:24.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just need to keep an eye on those brats\Nwho are overconfident in the powers\Nthey've been given and dare to defy God.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.99,0:08:28.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their plot would bring about the end of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.04,0:08:31.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The end of the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.49,0:08:35.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. We have to prevent that, whatever it takes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.62,0:08:39.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the only one who can protect everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.56,0:08:40.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You understand that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.50,0:08:43.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing to fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.87,0:08:49.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your power and my sense of relativity were made for each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.92,0:08:53.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you ever coming back?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.88,0:08:55.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'd love to get the gang together again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.62,0:08:57.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got Nagara, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.39,0:09:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, Nagara's giving it his all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.32,0:09:04.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's trying to prove to himself that he can stand up to the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.35,0:09:06.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our very own Nagara!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.16,0:09:16.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like playing it backwards goes against the rules of this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.04,0:09:19.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was thinking we could go back to before we went adrift,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.42,0:09:20.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I guess it's not that easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.98,0:09:24.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can see the past, but we can't change it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.35,0:09:28.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means that effects can't happen without their causes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.12,0:09:31.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.74,0:09:33.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, that one's no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.74,0:09:36.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been eaten by mold, and it's the wrong size.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.52,0:09:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.80,0:09:49.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You really are special.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.88,0:09:54.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We might be able to go home now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.82,0:09:58.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So you have a new project, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.01,0:10:01.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I do. I call it the "Director's Cut" project.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.03,0:10:03.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.32,0:10:10.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A director's cut is when a movie that has already been in theaters
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.87,0:10:10.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,gets re-edited, and becomes a remade production.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.00,0:10:14.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the same way, I'm thinking of having us do a director's cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.80,0:10:15.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of what?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.32,0:10:18.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of ourselves and this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.35,0:10:26.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are castaways who ended up in this world by mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.36,0:10:30.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And over here, we have another reel of film that Nagara found.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.62,0:10:36.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This film shows our own world,\Nwhere we're supposed to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.76,0:10:39.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, that takes me back!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.68,0:10:40.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you were a transfer student.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.95,0:10:42.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.14,0:10:47.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to paste ourselves in here where we're missing,\Nand re-edit our own world.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.52,0:10:50.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to remake our own world ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.90,0:10:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's gonna pull off something as ambitious as that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.03,0:10:55.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.38,0:10:57.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.87,0:11:02.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it's a hurdle we can't get over, Nagara is able to.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.42,0:11:09.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we can change the future as much as we like.{Natsume really going full "DO YOU GET IT YET" on this one lmfao}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.42,0:11:13.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't change the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.01,0:11:15.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What if the future is already decided?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.75,0:11:18.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We already know how it turns out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.75,0:11:22.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is knowing really all that great?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.56,0:11:27.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I {\i1}am{\i0} that great.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.72,0:11:31.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how impressive you are,\N you can't change the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.72,0:11:35.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You should use your power in a way that's more helpful to all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.49,0:11:38.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This shelter, you see, is actually an ark.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.69,0:11:43.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With it, I will save us all from the coming disaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.69,0:11:47.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not like we asked for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.64,0:11:48.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you say something?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.75,0:11:58.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara's right. Hoshi, we ought to—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.75,0:12:00.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if the outcome is set in stone,\NI'm not running from it.\NYeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.57,0:12:03.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cap, have I ever been wrong about anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.02,0:12:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't believe in keeping to the beaten path,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.02,0:12:11.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.\NBut even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.02,0:12:14.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then breathing a sigh of relief when you arrive safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.20,0:12:17.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not how you should live your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.46,0:12:23.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh dear.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.74,0:12:27.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nagara, I think it's about time to relocate to another world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.42,0:12:36.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's quit this, already.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.04,0:12:40.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how many power relics we collect,\Nwe'll never be able to beat Asakaze and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.49,0:12:43.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starting to wonder if we were wrong after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.19,0:12:56.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it true that you were able to change the world?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.01,0:12:59.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. It worked perfectly in our experiments,\Nfor the most part.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.40,0:13:00.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For the most part?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.01,0:13:05.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah... There are times when the editing works,\Nand times when it doesn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.45,0:13:08.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It seems like there's some kind of random chance at play.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.51,0:13:11.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure we'll be all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.20,0:13:12.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing strange is going to happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.68,0:13:14.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, nothing like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.11,0:13:17.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is based on the fact that only things that {\i1}can{\i0} happen {\i1}will{\i0} happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.91,0:13:19.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You being who you are isn't going to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.86,0:13:21.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.96,0:13:26.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be fine! You're not going to suddenly turn into a dog or anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.72,0:13:31.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For one thing, this world is set up so that things work in the students' favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.92,0:13:37.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are only students who went to {\i1}our{\i0} school going adrift?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.60,0:13:41.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's because the principal is God.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.32,0:13:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.15,0:13:45.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The principal? You mean {\i1}our{\i0} principal?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.36,0:13:50.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This drifting was brought about according to His will.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.08,0:13:53.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? But why would God be our principal?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.56,0:13:56.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing more than simple coincidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.47,0:13:59.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He just happened to be the principal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.09,0:14:00.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He just happened to be?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.75,0:14:05.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But even if that's so,\Nwhat is the point of us going adrift?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.62,0:14:06.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no point.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.32,0:14:08.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nil.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.00,0:14:16.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's from Ace. He says they want to meet up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.32,0:14:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?! Why now, after everything they put Nagara through?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.03,0:14:20.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let them come.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.88,0:14:22.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.80,0:14:27.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they've taken the steps to contacting us,\Nthey must have seen the error of their ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.62,0:14:30.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, if they're in trouble,\Nwe should extend a helping hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.18,0:14:31.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make them beg! Make them beg!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.56,0:14:33.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what the ark is for.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.61,0:14:39.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, this is where we'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.45,0:14:41.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is where we'll build our ark.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.82,0:14:43.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ark?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.00,0:14:46.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I have to save everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.32,0:14:47.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You understand, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.67,0:14:51.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see, I want to save all of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.74,0:14:54.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you sure we shouldn't be helping Rajdhani and the others?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.89,0:14:55.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.83,0:14:56.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.99,0:15:00.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because the way things are going,\Nit seems like we're never going home.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.35,0:15:01.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what if we don't?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.89,0:15:07.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if we never go home,\Nit has no bearing on our previous world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.61,0:15:09.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to save everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.36,0:15:13.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just want to save everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.21,0:15:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did they ask for your salvation?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.77,0:15:20.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure this is the way to go?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.71,0:15:24.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just doing exactly as you're told...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.34,0:15:27.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It isn't like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.54,0:15:34.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we get home tomorrow,\Nwe'll be just in time for our graduation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.21,0:15:37.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you think we could still graduate after missing this much school?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.12,0:15:40.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.09,0:15:53.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't fly anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.05,0:15:57.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Today's our graduation ceremony.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.86,0:16:03.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.54,0:16:12.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our shelter has now become an ark.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.20,0:16:18.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When will you finally understand?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.90,0:16:21.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give it up, already!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.80,0:16:35.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ms. Aki! Listen to me, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.22,0:16:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not possible for this project to cause the end of the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.98,0:16:41.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, it is ending!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.15,0:16:45.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A teacher?\NNo, that can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.15,0:16:46.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.05,0:16:49.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All that ever goes adrift are the school and its students.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.32,0:16:50.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.34,0:16:56.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no choice but for you to stay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.19,0:16:58.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.91,0:17:31.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is Nagara doing this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.78,0:17:35.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The world really has changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.32,0:17:37.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Great, looks like it worked.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.92,0:17:41.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's move on to the project. Agreed?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.47,0:17:43.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.60,0:17:45.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's give it a try.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.20,0:17:47.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They said they're ready whenever.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.80,0:17:50.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're ready here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.40,0:17:53.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's all go home together!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.01,0:17:54.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.45,0:18:11.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Honestly, what are we going to do about your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.15,0:18:14.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can't you just make a decision on your own already?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.76,0:18:17.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need to do more than just discuss this over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.45,0:18:19.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.05,0:18:23.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Miss!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.05,0:18:23.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When did that get there?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.75,0:18:25.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a dead bird at the front gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.88,0:18:27.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's gross. Please do something about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.79,0:18:29.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.17,0:18:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not right to take things out on those weaker than you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.72,0:18:37.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, that isn't what I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.94,0:18:48.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.19,0:18:48.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The light...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.07,0:18:51.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The light is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.75,0:18:53.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The light?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.11,0:18:54.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one you've been talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.56,0:18:55.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.82,0:18:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were right after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.75,0:19:13.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are all no longer needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.75,0:19:26.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Asakaze!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.77,0:19:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.56,0:19:54.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm... here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.71,0:20:41.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a pity.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.13,0:20:46.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You always have to screen the future to see what will happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.36,0:20:43.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.36,0:20:47.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were not creating worlds.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.87,0:20:52.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You were just an observer,\N opening boxes of possibilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.87,0:20:58.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This world exists because you are here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.46,0:21:03.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are simply copies.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.34,0:21:05.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.89,0:21:10.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.89,0:21:10.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were not chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.37,0:21:07.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's another me here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.02,0:21:13.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We no longer have a place to go home to.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.45,0:21:18.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I get it. This wasn't us going adrift—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.36,0:21:29.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was God rolling the dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.12,0:21:36.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you really think that you were the only special ones?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.38,0:21:39.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They ended up failing, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.03,0:21:42.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were so close, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.76,0:21:46.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Congratulations on your graduation!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.35,0:22:01.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure that this was for the best?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.12,0:22:04.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. The world has been preserved.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.43,0:22:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.20,0:22:08.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It didn't work.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.06,0:22:10.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not your fault, Nagara.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.86,0:22:13.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the end, it was a matter of probability.{(QC) remove comma}\NThat's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.72,0:22:17.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was a chance that we would become the originals.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.89,0:22:19.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've underestimated you, Nagara.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.33,0:22:24.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, I thought you said there was still time.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.39,0:22:28.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eight months fits within the margin of error of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.58,0:22:32.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no chance left for me, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.19,0:22:40.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have to get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.19,0:22:46.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was dead.\NHuh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.75,0:22:52.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what could the light have been, then?
